WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:06.845
Two feeds reach a payments service: card events and bank events.

2
00:00:06.845 --> 00:00:10.277
Each marble is one item, and time runs left to right.

3
00:00:10.277 --> 00:00:13.451
Reactor has four ways to make one stream of them.

4
00:00:13.567 --> 00:00:19.021
merge subscribes to both at once, and passes on each item the moment it arrives.

5
00:00:19.021 --> 00:00:20.044
What comes out?

6
00:00:22.333 --> 00:00:25.078
Arrival order: 1, x, 2, y, 3, z.

7
00:00:25.078 --> 00:00:29.280
It's done at 120, when both feeds have completed.

8
00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:31.247
concat takes turns.

9
00:00:31.247 --> 00:00:35.217
It subscribes to bank only after card completes, at 100.

10
00:00:35.217 --> 00:00:37.344
Where do the bank events land?

11
00:00:39.633 --> 00:00:47.491
Bank starts its own clock when it is subscribed, so its events come at 140, 180 and 220.

12
00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:53.495
If card never completes, like a live Kafka feed, concat never subscribes to bank at all.

13
00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:58.464
zip pairs by position: first with first, second with second.

14
00:00:58.464 --> 00:01:00.380
When does each pair come out?

15
00:01:02.667 --> 00:01:05.860
1 waits for x, and the pair goes out at 40.

16
00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:08.756
Then 2 and y at 80, and 3 and z at 120.

17
00:01:08.756 --> 00:01:14.697
zip completes when either side completes, and drops the extras of a longer side.

18
00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:17.834
Now bank completes with nothing at all.

19
00:01:17.834 --> 00:01:19.068
What does zip emit?

20
00:01:21.367 --> 00:01:21.964
Nothing.

21
00:01:21.964 --> 00:01:23.681
No value, and no error.

22
00:01:23.681 --> 00:01:28.384
Bank has completed, so zip completes at once, and cancels card.

23
00:01:28.500 --> 00:01:30.062
Mono.zip does the same.

24
00:01:30.062 --> 00:01:36.108
One lookup finds no limit, and the whole quote completes empty, with nothing in the logs.

25
00:01:37.133 --> 00:01:40.894
combineLatest also waits until each side has one item.

26
00:01:40.894 --> 00:01:45.420
Then every new item goes out with the latest from the other side.

27
00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:46.604
How many results?

28
00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:49.281
Five.

29
00:01:49.281 --> 00:01:52.178
2 pairs with x again, and then with y.

30
00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:56.067
The latest value stays in use until it is replaced.

31
00:01:57.767 --> 00:02:05.347
In code, give every zipped source an answer for empty: an error with switchIfEmpty, or a value with defaultIfEmpty.

32
00:02:07.133 --> 00:02:09.657
So ask two questions about any combinator.

33
00:02:09.657 --> 00:02:11.940
When does it subscribe to each source?

34
00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:15.665
And what does it do when one source completes early, or empty?

35
00:02:16.367 --> 00:02:17.252
Quick check.

36
00:02:17.252 --> 00:02:24.257
Mono.zip of a write that completes empty after 20 milliseconds, and a rate call that takes 100.

37
00:02:24.257 --> 00:02:26.691
What does the zip emit, and when?
